ai_system_id:
A decision rule, pi(), is (alpha, p)-Marginal-balanced with respect to beta if Fairness f follows the equation:

f_FP (pi) = the sum (for a=1,y=0,z) | the sum (for all x) of pi(a | x)?[P_beta (x, z|y) ? P_beta (x|y)P_beta (z|y)] | p <= alpha;

where P_beta is the marginal probability of the policy, i.e., the probability of beta (P_beta) = the integral over all possible values of beta of the probability of theta given beta, times the probability density function of beta  with respect to theta. Similarly, marginal FN Balance, f_FN and marginal FPFN Balance, f_FPFN can be defined.

